MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_001: There were some rumors of eerie rumblings coming\nfrom around here somewhere.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_002: This place is desolate, but I don't see anything too\nsuspicious yet.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_003: Uwah! I guess those are the rumbles!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_004: Thought I heard a voice! Hey, Ultand. Whatcha\ndoing out here?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_005: Goliath? I could ask you the same thing, "Butcher"!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_006: But, did you feel that rumbling just now?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_007: Rumbling? Oh, you must have heard me training!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_008: There's a great big rock over there. I just SLAM into\nit as hard as I can!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_009: Used to do it to pillars back in Dagsion. They made\nme stop 'cause I was cracking 'em. Heh heh heh.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_010: Quite a unique training method. I'll give you that.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_011: Hey, you've got a cut on your forehead.\nYou're bleeding!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_012: Oh! Guess I do. No biggie, it'll heal.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_013: You can't be too careful, even with a scratch. Here,\nlet me take care of it.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_014: Huh? Uh, OK...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_015: How come you're not scared of me? You weren't\nafraid when we met either.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_016: Relax. It's not that you're not a big, scary guy. It's just\nthat my instinct to help the helpless takes over.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_017: I don't think anyone's ever been nice to me before!\nNot someone I barely know, at least. Feels weird.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_018: Hehe. Well, I've just read lots of fairy tales, classic\nlove stories where the girl falls for the dangerous guy.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_019: A love what? Ya lost me.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_020: Never heard a bard tell a tale? There are some great\nones, like...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_021: So they cross paths, can't stand each other at first,\nand then get together. Pretty great story, huh?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_022: Huh... You look a lot less serious than usual.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_023: Haha. I guess I'm being a little childish. I got kind of\ncarried away with the story. I'm a little embarrassed.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_024: Naw, I-I-I mean, it's just... You look kinda...\nWell, kinda...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_025: Cuuu—uuu... Could you excuse me?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_026: You OK? Does your scratch still hurt?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_027: Ngaaah!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_C_028: What's with him? Is my storytelling that boring?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_001: I've touched base with a lot of people today. Now I\njust need to find a nice souvenir for Aurora.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_002: Ah, there you are, Ultand! I been looking for you.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_003: Ah, Goliath!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_004: Here! It's a present!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_005: It's a...comb? A...giant...comb?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_006: You've been so nice to me, I wanted to do somethin'\nnice for you.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_007: Wasn't sure what would be good... But I figured,\nat least you could use this!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_008: Oh, I'm...happy to have this. It's just kind of...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_009: Aww. It was weird for me to get you something,\nhuh? I'm sorry.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_010: No, no, no! It's just a lot bigger than the comb I\nnormally use. That's all.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_011: Oh... Yeah, I guess you got those tiny hands.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_012: Huh? That sound... Oh, no! That horse is rampaging!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_013: Get behind me!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_014: Huh?!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_015: Is it gone? That was scary!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_016: Sorry, didn't mean to pull you outta the way\nso rough.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_017: It's fine. That frazzled me, but I'm relieved it's over.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_018: Oh, OK! I thought you mighta got hurt.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_019: Not a scratch, thanks to you, Goliath. You saved me.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_020: Good! Now I guess I'd better get ahold of that\nrunaway horse!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_021: So Goliath has a soft side. He was so quick to help.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_022: Oh! The comb broke! But I think I can fix it if I\nget creative.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_023: Piece of cake! Bwahaha!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_024: Aw, did the comb snap?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_033: Yes. The horse broke your nice gift.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_034: But the good news is, a piece of it is just the right\nsize now, if I can get a craftsman to polish it for me.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_025: You sure? I can buy you a new one!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_026: Nah, I'll just take good care of this one.\nThanks again, Goliath.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_027: Oh... Don't mention it.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_028: Well, I'd better get going. I've heard a lot of good\nstories from folks today, so I think I'll head home.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_029: More of those fables we were talkin' about?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_030: Some, but also just everyday small talk. I gather up\nbits from here and there to entertain Aurora.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_031: I gotcha. Well, if it's something you're interested in,\nI bet I will be too!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_B_032: Hehe. Sure! See you again sometime.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_001: But he realized that picking up a big sack of money\nwas just a dream. So he gave up.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_002: After that, the husband's whole attitude changed,\nand he started saving money more diligently.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_003: Hehehe. All because of his wife! Smart stuff,\nthat woman.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_004: You're really getting into this. That's wonderful!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_005: Well, my life's been mostly fightin'. I don't get to\nthinking about other folks' lives too often.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_006: But when you talk about 'em, they always sound\nso interesting!
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_007: Hehe. Now you're just flattering me. I think all my\nstories have done is given you a silver tongue.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_008: Naw, nothin' like that. You wanna tell me another?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_009: I wonder which one I should tell you next.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_010: How about a fable? One you really like?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_011: Oh! I just heard a new love story from a bard. Let's\ngo with that one.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_012: Once upon a time, in a far-off town, there was a\nmighty warrior, a man of great strength.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_013: But he was rough around the edges, and not so good\nwith other people.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_014: However, there was one woman who admired him.\nShe just couldn't resist the urge to help the helpless.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_015: {SetColor=Gray}Uh-oh. The people in this story might seem a little\ntoo similar to me and Goliath.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_016: {SetColor=Gray}What if he gets it into his head that I'm carrying a\ntorch for him?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_017: {SetColor=Gray}I guess that wouldn't be so bad.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_018: Hey, Ultand. This story's givin' me an idea.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_019: Oh? Aaand what are you thinking?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_020: This warrior guy in the fable. I mean...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_021: Yes?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_022: Is he based on a real guy? 'Cause if he is, I might\nhave to fight him.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_023: U-uhhh...
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_024: That...is a detail I don't know about.
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_025: Huh! Guess ya can't always tell. Wanna tell me the\nrest of it?
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_026: {SetColor=Gray}He didn't pick up on the nuances in the slightest.\nPerhaps the story didn't trigger anything for him.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Hur_Gol_A_027: {SetColor=Gray}There it is... My instinct to help the helpless is\nkicking in again.{SetColor=Default}